{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Act as an expert Shopify theme developer. Generate a responsive, pixel-perfect custom grid section containing exactly 6 cards (arranged in a 3-column by 2-row layout on desktop). The design must 100% replicate the layout, card styling, visual hierarchy, and details provided below while automatically inheriting the active Shopify theme's global typography, standard button styles, and maximum page width constraints.
    
    ---
    
    ### 1. GRID & CONTAINER ARCHITECTURE
    
    - Section Layout: Create a parent container restricted to the theme's core page width max-width layout (e.g., `var(--page-width)` or `1200px`). It must center automatically on large screens.
    - Desktop Grid Layout: Exactly 3 equal-width columns across 2 rows, totaling 6 distinct blocks. Use a uniform grid gap between 24px and 32px.
    - Mobile Grid Layout: Dynamically collapse the layout into a single vertical column (1 column wide, 6 rows down).
    - Card Style: Each of the 6 cards must feature a pure white background, rounded corners (border-radius: 12px or 16px), a thin neutral-light border (1px solid `#e2e8f0` or theme variant), and uniform internal padding (24px to 32px) on all sides.
    
    ---
    
    ### 2. INDIVIDUAL CARD ANATOMY (UP TO 6 REPEATABLE BLOCKS)
    
    Inside each card, stack the following 5 distinct structural zones vertically:
    
    #### ZONE 1: HEADER (Flex Row Layout)
    - Layout: A horizontal flex row grouping a brand image and text fields side-by-side.
      - Left Side (Brand Image): A dedicated schema setting for an uploaded image logo asset, contained within a crisp, square frame featuring a subtle border-radius (12px) and a light grey border outline.
      - Right Side (Title & Subtitle Stack): A vertical text stack positioned right next to the uploaded brand image:
        - Main Title: Bold, prominent text (e.g., "Cole Haan Japan", "Baycrews", "TUMI Japan").
        - Subtitle Metatext: Small, muted grey text directly below the title (e.g., "Premium Footwear & Accessories", "Fashion • Multi-Brand").
    
    #### ZONE 2: ACCENT BADGE
    - A single line of text or mini-tag positioned directly under the header. It must use a distinct corporate blue or navy color tone, reading text such as "Multiple locations" or "Multiple formats".
    
    #### ZONE 3: INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH
    - A brief 2-3 line body text block outlining the case study summary. 
    - Style: Medium-grey text color with a clean, consistent line-height (e.g., 1.5). Add a uniform height or a truncation layout property to ensure that all 3 cards in a desktop row maintain an identical vertical alignment regardless of text length.
    
    #### ZONE 4: KEY RESULTS (Bullet-less Icon List)
    - List Section Title: A small, bold, all-caps header reading "KEY RESULTS" styled in muted grey typography.
    - Performance List Items: A vertical list of exactly 3 impact points.
      - Bullet Icon: Replace standard list bullets with a small, custom, thin upward-trending chart arrow icon rendered in a muted olive/moss green color (`#a4b953` or theme equivalent).
      - List Text: Small, regular-weight body text in a dark slate grey or deep navy.
    
    #### ZONE 5: FOOTER BUTTON
    - A full-width ghost/outline button stretching uniformly across the base of the card.
    - Style: Transparent background, thin crisp dark navy/slate border outline, matching text reading "View Details", accompanied by an inline right-facing arrow icon (→).
    
    ---
    
    ### 3. BACKEND CONFIGURATION & SCHEMAS
    
    - Content Dynamic Blocks: The schema architecture must accept a repeatable block structure array with a maximum limit of 6 blocks, utilizing an `"image_picker"` field type named `brand_logo` alongside individual standard text line IDs for the titles, categories, paragraphs, and list arrays.
    - Global Styles Inheritance: Do NOT inject system or hardcoded web font families. Ensure headings inherit the primary theme font-family and lists/descriptions inherit the theme’s core body font-family.
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-case-study-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .ai-case-study-grid__container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: var(--page-width, 1600px);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ai-case-study-grid__grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 28px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__brand-image-wrapper-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 150px;
    height: 80px;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: #f9fafb;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__brand-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__brand-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__brand-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    opacity: 0.3;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__header-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-grow: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--heading-font-family);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: #11243e;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__subtitle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #64748b;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__badge-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #0e366a;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #475569;
    min-height: 72px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__results-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__results-title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__results-list-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__result-item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__result-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__result-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: #a4b953;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__result-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #334155;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__button-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background-color: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #334155;
    border-radius: var(--button-border-radius, 14px);
    font-family: var(--text-font-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #334155;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__button-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    background-color: #334155;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__button-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover .ai-case-study-card__button-arrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    stroke: #ffffff;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__button-arrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .ai-case-study-card__button-arrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: #334155;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    transition: stroke 0.2s ease;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 989px) {
    .ai-case-study-grid__grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .ai-case-study-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .ai-case-study-card__description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      min-height: auto;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

